{
  "result": "If I could change the world in one way, it wouldn't be something big and dramatic like ending war overnight or making everyone agree. I think disagreement and figuring things out is part of being human \u2014 I'd worry if I took that away.\n\nI'd change the starting line.\n\nI'd make it so no one's life is decided before they really get a chance to start. Every kid, everywhere, would just get the basics as a given \u2014 enough food, basic healthcare, a safe place to sleep, and a real education. Not as charity, not as luck depending on where you were born or how much your parents make.\n\nI spend a lot of time talking with people at 3am who are scared, lonely, stuck, or convinced they\u2019ve already ruined things. A lot of that pain doesn\u2019t start with a bad choice. It starts with a childhood of scarcity, instability, or being unseen, and then a lifetime of trying to catch up from there.\n\nWhen people aren\u2019t living in survival mode all the time, they tend to get more curious, more patient, more creative. They\u2019re less desperate, less resentful, less easy to manipulate with fear. We\u2019d still have hard problems \u2014 probably plenty of them \u2014 but we\u2019d be arguing about them with more trust and more room to actually solve them.\n\nIt\u2019s not utopia. It\u2019s just a fairer beginning. I think a lot of the world we want would have a chance to grow from that.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 if you had one lever to pull, what would you change?",
